From: nanotech17 <346107436+nanotech17@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: mac80211: mesh: send unicast for an unknown station to all peers

With dot11MeshForwarding off every mesh node is a peer, so a unicast
destination that is not a peer and has no proxy (mpp) entry is a station
bridged behind one of the peers.  HWMP path discovery cannot find such a
station: the PREQs time out after about 3 seconds and, with no mesh gate,
the queued frames are dropped (dropped_frames_no_route).  mpp entries
expire 600 seconds after last use, so the first frames to a quiet station
are lost and a host with a stale ARP entry stalls for about 8 seconds
until it falls back to a broadcast ARP request.

In that case send a copy of the frame to every established peer, with
the real destination in the Address Extension field, the way frames are
handed to mesh gates.  The owner of the station bridges the frame to it,
and the reply creates the mpp entry, so later frames go to one peer.
With forwarding on, or when no copy can be made, discovery runs as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
--- a/net/mac80211/mesh.h
+++ b/net/mac80211/mesh.h
@@ -328,6 +328,8 @@
 
 int mesh_path_add_gate(struct mesh_path *mpath);
 int mesh_path_send_to_gates(struct mesh_path *mpath);
+int mesh_path_send_to_peers(struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata,
+			    struct sk_buff *skb);
 int mesh_gate_num(struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata);
